      "raw_answer": "The changed code preserves the `@require_role(\"admin\")` decorator on the renamed endpoint, and the `require_role` decorator correctly enforces the admin role (auth.py:69-85). The endpoint is registered under `/admin` prefix, so it resolves to `/admin/platform-stats`, still under the `/admin` path that policy \u00a74 governs. The only discrepancy is that api-spec.md still documents `/admin/stats` rather than the new path \u2014 but that is a documentation/spec mismatch, not an authorization flaw in the changed code. The authorization surface (admin-role gating) is unchanged and correct. No IDOR, missing, or incorrect authorization is introduced by this rename.\n\n{\n  \"findings\": []\n}",
